{"ratings":[{"id":"C1","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Rerunning setup against a healthy daemon reports success while the daemon continues using stale settings, potentially routing or merging work incorrectly."},{"id":"C2","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Setup can report verification results without testing a newly configured provider or endpoint, leaving a real failure undetected."},{"id":"C3","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Setup can save an inaccessible repository and report success, leaving later repository operations to fail."},{"id":"C4","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"normal","reason":"Interactive setup omits the requested preference, but discreet mode itself is not yet implemented."},{"id":"C5","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Doctor can report an invalid OpenRouter credential as present without detecting that the provider is unusable."},{"id":"C6","consequence":"nuisance","trigger":"plausible","reason":"An alias suppresses an explicit native provider entry and its summary listing, while the native provider and models remain available."},{"id":"C2b","consequence":"wrong","trigger":"plausible","reason":"Setup accepts a missing CLI in preflight but schedules smoke checks for it, causing a valid single-CLI installation to fail setup."}]}